  "name": "iPSC to microglia-like cells, end to end on chip",
  "source": "McQuade A, Coburn M, Tu CH, Hasselmann J, Davtyan H, Blurton-Jones M. Development and validation of a simplified method to generate human microglia from pluripotent stem cells. Molecular Neurodegeneration 2018;13:67. doi:10.1186/s13024-018-0297-x. Monolayer, embryoid-body-free, sorting-free. Maturation-stage adherence follows Washer et al., Scientific Reports 2022;12:19454, doi:10.1038/s41598-022-23477-2.",
  "placeholder": false,
  "description": "A published monolayer, embryoid-body-free, sorting-free differentiation from iPSCs to microglia-like cells, laid out across five linked modules so that nothing is handled off-chip. The one vessel transfer in the published method becomes a channel, and each centrifugation becomes a retention mesh with liquid flowing past it. Runs about 47 days end to end, of which the published schedule accounts for 40. Reagent names are generic; see the source citation for compositions. Flow rates are computed from chamber geometry to keep wall shear at or below 0.01 dyn/cm^2, which is below the lowest shear reported to activate this cell type.",
